some first-grade students are the children of migrant workers, but their household registration is not in S City. This does not provide any information about third-grade students being children of migrant workers. Therefore, we cannot conclude that some children of migrant workers are third-grade students.\n\n**Option C: Some students with household registration in this city are third-grade students**.\n- The context clearly states that all third-grade students are registered in S City. Therefore, it is correct to say that some students with household registration in S City are third-grade students.\n\n**Option D: Some first-grade students are not children of migrant workers**.\n- The context states that some first-grade students are the children of migrant workers, but their household registration is not in S City. This means that these first-grade students are not registered in S City. Therefore, we cannot conclude that some first-grade students are not children of migrant workers.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nBased on the given context, the correct conclusion is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
