      "text": " B\n\nOption A: Li is engaged in the steel business. During this period, the steel is very tight. The material company also requires cash to pick up the goods, and the payment cannot be received at that time. This time, he wants to buy 5 tons of deformed steel bar. According to the pricing, he paid 14,000 yuan. He didn't get the required steel until a month later.\n- **Analysis**: Li paid 14,000 yuan in advance to secure the purchase of steel. However, he did not receive the steel until a month later. This situation does not fit the definition of a deposit because the payment was made in advance, but the goods were not delivered until after the payment was made. This is more of a prepayment or advance payment rather than a deposit.\n\nOption B: Fenghua company in Qiqihar ordered 38 tons of beef from Shenda company in Inner Mongolia. Due to the large sales, Shenda is a small company, and its working capital is not enough, so it is difficult to acquire the required amount of beef. Considering the actual situation of Shenda company, Fenghua company paid 50,000 yuan in advance to Shenda company in order to make the intention as soon as possible.\n- **Analysis**: Fenghua company paid 50,000 yuan in advance to secure the beef order. This fits the definition of a deposit because it is an advance payment made to guarantee the performance of the contract. The payment is made in advance to ensure the contract is fulfilled.\n\nOption C: Changhai company signed a contract with Zhiming oil factory for the production and marketing of salad oil. The contract stipulates that Zhiming oil factory should supply 80 tons of high-quality salad oil to Changhai company within 5 months after the signing of the contract. During this period, Zhiming oil factory had a mechanical accident, resulting in the shutdown of the factory for 3 months. Due to the failure to deliver on time, Zhiming oil factory paid 30,000 yuan to Changhai company according to the contract.\n- **Analysis**: This situation involves a breach of contract where Zhiming oil factory failed to deliver the goods on time. The payment of 30,000 yuan is a penalty or compensation for the breach, not an advance payment to secure the contract.\n\nOption D: At an order meeting, the deputy general manager of Aetna trading company signed a contract for the purchase and sale of flax silk with a printing and dyeing factory, with a total contract amount of 7.8 million yuan. According to the agreement between the two sides, the printing and dyeing factory should pay Aetna trading company 1.56 million yuan according to 20% of the contract amount as a good faith to perform the contract, but the printing and dyeing factory was very short of funds, so it couldn't get so much money at the moment, so it pieced together to pay 1 million yuan.\n- **Analysis**: The printing and dyeing factory paid 1 million yuan, which is 14% of the total contract amount (1.56 million yuan). This is not an advance payment to secure the contract but rather a partial payment made due to financial constraints. It does not fit the definition of a deposit.\n\n### Conclusion:\nBased on the analysis, the correct option that fits the definition of a deposit is **Option B**.",
