ual support.\n\n2. **Option B:**.\n   - Lao Wu visits his parents every day for many years, taking care of their lives meticulously.\n   - The elderly are very pleased with his care.\n   - This option indicates that Lao Wu is providing emotional and practical support to his parents, which is also a form of spiritual support.\n\n3. **Option C:**.\n   - Dean Li invited the little red flower orchestra of Chaoyang Primary School to the sunset red nursing home.\n   - The children\'s laughter and wonderful performances brought endless happiness to the elderly.\n   - This option shows that the elderly are receiving joy and entertainment through the performances of children, which is a form of spiritual support.\n\n4. **Option D:**.\n   - Lao Jiang\'s mother is in her 70s and refuses to accept her old age.\n   - Lao Jiang signed up for a ballroom dancing training class for his mother.\n   - Lao Jiang follows her every time she goes to class to prevent her from getting angry and to ensure her safety.\n   - This option describes Lao Jiang taking care of his mother\'s physical activities and safety, but it does not mention any form of emotional or spiritual support. Instead, it focuses on physical and safety concerns. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
