messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nZhao Ming, Qian Hong and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University and Beijing normal University. About which school they were admitted to, the students made the following guesses: classmate A guessed: Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing normal University. Classmate B guess: Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing normal University and Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University. Classmate C guess: Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. As a result, the students' guesses were half right.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct admission?\n# Options:\nA) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, tsinghua university and beijing normal university respectively.\nB) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to tsinghua university, beijing normal university and peking university respectively.\nC) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to beijing normal university, tsinghua university and peking university respectively.\nD) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, beijing normal university and tsinghua university respectively.. I think the correct option is: B\n", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to analyze the guesses made by Classmate A, Classmate B, and Classmate C, and determine which combination of admissions satisfies the condition that exactly half of the guesses are correct.\n\nLet's break down the guesses:.\n\n1. **Classmate A's Guess:**.\n   - Zhao Ming was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n   - Sun Jie was admitted to Beijing Normal University.\n\n2. **Classmate B's Guess:**.\n   - Zhao Ming was admitted to Beijing Normal University.\n   - Qian Hong was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\n3. **Classmate C's Guess:**.\n   - Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University.\n   - Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\nWe know that exactly half of the guesses are correct, which means 1 out of 3 guesses is correct.\n\nLet's analyze each option to see which one fits the condition:.\n\n### Option A: Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University, and Beijing Normal University respectively.\n- Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua) and Sun Jie (Beijing Normal) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal) and Qian Hong (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking) and Sun Jie (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- This option results in 3 correct guesses, which does not satisfy the condition of exactly half being correct.\n\n### Option B: Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Tsinghua University, Beijing Normal University, and Peking University respectively.\n- Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua) and Sun Jie (Beijing Normal) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal) and Qian Hong (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking) and Sun Jie (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- This option results in 3 correct guesses, which does not satisfy the condition of exactly half being correct.\n\n### Option C: Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Beijing Normal University, Tsinghua University, and Peking University respectively.\n- Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua) and Sun Jie (Beijing Normal) - 0 correct.\n- Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal) and Qian Hong (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking) and Sun Jie (Tsinghua) - 0 correct.\n- This option results in 1 correct guess, which does not satisfy the condition of exactly half being correct.\n\n### Option D: Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Beijing Normal University, and Tsinghua University respectively.\n- Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua) and Sun Jie (Beijing Normal) - 0 correct.\n- Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal) and Qian Hong (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking) and Sun Jie (Tsinghua) - 1 correct.\n- This option results in 2 correct guesses, which satisfies the condition of exactly half being correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
