ects.\n\n**C) A place uses a lot of fossil fuels, and the temperature in the area is significantly higher than the surrounding areas.**.\n- This scenario involves human activities (use of fossil fuels) leading to a significant change in temperature. This is a clear example of environmental effects.\n\n**D) A coastal city reclaimed the sea to build an island, and a small town with a capacity of 70,000 people was built on the island.**.\n- This scenario describes a human activity (reclaiming sea to build an island) but does not explicitly mention any changes in the structure or function of the environmental system. It simply describes the creation of a new land area and a town. This does not directly relate to environmental effects as defined.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nThe option that does not describe environmental effects is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
